# Unity — paste into the "Stack-specific rules" section of .gitignore.
#
# Source: compared line by line with GitHub's Unity.gitignore
# (https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/Unity.gitignore, read 2026-10-15). The one
# deliberate difference: the Visual Scripting rule below ignores the whole generated folder,
# where GitHub's template ignores three generated paths inside it.
#
# bootstrap.sh copies files; it does not merge into an existing .gitignore, so this is a
# manual step. Two things to get right:
#
#   1. These rules are ROOTED AT /unity/ because the Unity project is a subfolder. If your
#      Unity project IS the repository root, remove the /unity prefix from every line.
#   2. The `*.csproj` / `*.sln` rules below are global — Unity regenerates its own. If you
#      have hand-written solution or project files elsewhere in the repo, re-include them in
#      the block at the very END of .gitignore. Git applies the LAST matching rule, so a
#      re-include placed above these lines does nothing (docs/GOTCHAS.md).

/unity/[Ll]ibrary/
/unity/[Tt]emp/
/unity/[Oo]bj/
/unity/[Bb]uild/
/unity/[Bb]uilds/
/unity/[Ll]ogs/
/unity/.utmp/
/unity/.gradle/
/unity/UIElementsSchema/
/unity/[Uu]ser[Ss]ettings/
/unity/[Mm]emoryCaptures/
/unity/[Rr]ecordings/
*.log

# Blender working files
*.blend1
*.blend1.meta

# Autogenerated IDE project files — Unity regenerates these
